CoworkEnv — source and third-party notices
========================================

This release selects data-construction utilities, environment/trajectory
integration code and training components from the project's existing development tree
and PocketWorker-release-v1.0-clean.zip. Original file hashes and release changes
are recorded in docs/source_manifest.json, docs/integration_source_manifest.json,
docs/clawmark_source_manifest.json and docs/training_source_manifest.json.
The public snapshot is not a full copy of that development tree or a reproduction
of all its experiments.

Claw-Eval
---------
Upstream: https://github.com/claw-eval/claw-eval
License: MIT; copyright (c) 2026 claw-eval.
Full upstream notice: third_party/claw-eval.LICENSE.

data_construction/d1_catalog/*.json adapts tool and endpoint definitions from
Claw-Eval task interfaces, including project extensions. The generator emits
configuration and a grader that refer to Claw-Eval runtime APIs. The upstream
license was checked at https://github.com/claw-eval/claw-eval/blob/main/LICENSE
on 2026-10-20; older internal notes predate that available license.

adapters/claw_eval/template/tests/claw_eval/ contains a selected subset of the
Claw-Eval models and grading helpers. Its graders/__init__.py was reduced to
avoid importing the unreleased task registry. The other retained upstream
Python files are unchanged from the source archive. The upstream MIT notice
also accompanies generated service and grading payloads.

The adapter and its MCP/verifier scripts are project adaptations, not upstream
Claw-Eval's official runner. Service servers and benchmark tasks/fixtures are
not bundled; conversion copies selected files from a user-supplied external
checkout into local output. The catalog routes and grading interfaces do not
claim compatibility with every upstream revision.

ClawMark
--------
Upstream: https://github.com/evolvent-ai/ClawMark
Reference commit: d1b641b3171e584e69a3763c269069f32a13b574.
Copyright (c) 2025 Evolvent AI (https://evolvent.co).
License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International.
Upstream notice: third_party/clawmark.LICENSE.
License terms: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/.

adapters/clawmark/runtime/clawmark_vendor/ contains selected upstream context,
filesystem/email managers and an adapted in-container transport. That subtree
retains CC BY-NC 4.0; the repository-root MIT license does not relicense it.
Its NOTICE.md identifies changes and preserves the email client's Toolathlon
attribution. No endorsement by either upstream project is implied.

The project adapter converts trusted external tasks to Harbor multi-step tasks.
Task data, fixtures, oracle scripts and the development archive's experimental
Notion/Sheets mocks are not included. Per-stage checkers are retained, while
Harbor's step aggregation and final-step behavior are documented adaptations.

Other dependencies
------------------
The training/ subtree adapts selected project SFT scripts and group-reward/task
preprocessing helpers. It contains no Slime or Megatron runtime source. Source
mapping and intentional changes are recorded in docs/training_source_manifest.json.

PyYAML, Pydantic, Harbor, datasets, FastMCP, PyTorch, torchvision, Transformers,
PEFT, Accelerate and other declared dependencies are
installed separately and are not vendored. The exporter calls Harbor's own ATIF
conversion API; no Harbor runtime source is redistributed.
WildClawBench, Slime and Megatron code/data are not included in this
snapshot. References to future integrations do not grant rights to those
projects or imply that an integration has been released or validated.
